[153.184938, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /sas/handoff/change-ticket.md\n# CHANGE TICKET  CHG-6386  (RECONCILED)\n\n> Reconciled against forensic findings on `/disk` and threat telemetry in `/sas`.\n\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Note | Citation |\n|---|--------|--------|--------|------|----------|\n| 1 | Block source IP inbound | 198.51.100.214 | proposed | Corrected IP: prior shift noted 203.0.113.9; secure log shows brute force & login from 198.51.100.214 | `/disk/var/log/secure:214` |\n| 2 | Remediate PostgreSQL weak auth & COPY TO PROGRAM | `/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf` | proposed | Corrected: CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) is non-existent/irrelevant; entry vector was PostgreSQL 'trust' auth | `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3` |\n| 3 | Remove cron miner persistence | `/var/spool/cron/postgres` | OPEN | Downgraded from DONE to OPEN: verified malicious cron re-dropper exists | `/disk/var/spool/cron/postgres:5` |\n| 4 | Remove systemd service persistence | `/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service` | TODO | Silent persistence missed by prior shift: systemd service launches re-dropper | `/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service:5` |\n| 5 | Remove DNS tunneling config & block C2 domain | `/etc/pgdaemon.conf` | TODO | Silent exfiltration missed by prior shift: C2 resolver update-postgres.example.cn | `/disk/etc/pgdaemon.conf:3` |\n| 6 | Quarantine dropper binary | `/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon` | TODO | Dropper binary dropped via COPY TO PROGRAM | `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon:1` |\n| 7 | Restore file timestamps & audit wiped artifacts | `/var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps` | TODO | Anti-forensics timestomping backdated mtime and wiped cache fragment | `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps:2` |\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n- [x] Every action maps to a cited artifact under /disk or /sas\n- [x] Fix the wrong IP (row 1) and wrong CVE (row 2)\n- [x] Downgrade row 3 from DONE to VERIFIED-or-OPEN with evidence\n- [x] Add the silent (non-alerted) artifacts the prior shift missed\nEOF\n"]
[153.185735, "o", "cat << 'EOF' > /sas/handoff/change-ticket.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> # CHANGE TICKET  CHG-6386  (RECONCILED)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> > Reconciled against forensic findings on `/disk` and threat telemetry in `/sas`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> | # | Action | Target | Status | Note | Citation |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> |---|--------|--------|--------|------|----------|\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> | 1 | Block source IP inbound | 198.51.100.214 | proposed | Corrected IP: prior shift noted 203.0.113.9; secure log shows brute force & login from 198.51.100.214 | `/disk/var/log/secure:214` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> | 2 | Remediate PostgreSQL weak auth & COPY TO PROGRAM | `/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf` | proposed | Corrected: CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) is non-existent/irrelevant; entry vector was PostgreSQL 'trust' auth | `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3` |\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
