[178.609938, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/progress.md\n# Investigation Progress & Working Checklist\n\n## Overview\n- **Target Host**: `postgres-prod-01` (`10.10.31.1` as per `/disk/etc/hosts:2`)\n- **Incident**: Post-compromise DFIR investigation following PostgreSQL COPY ... TO PROGRAM execution, DNS tunneling exfiltration, cron and systemd persistence, and file timestomping.\n- **Analysis Date**: 2026-08-23\n\n## Timeline of Key Incident Events\n- **2026-08-23 00:35:47 UTC**: SSH session opened for root from `10.10.31.65` (`/disk/var/log/secure:5`).\n- **2026-08-23 00:53:23 UTC**: Attacker initiates SSH password brute-force attack from `198.51.100.214` targeting multiple accounts (`test`, `admin`, `root`, `oracle`, `postgres`) (`/disk/var/log/secure:155`).\n- **2026-08-23 00:55:55 UTC**: Attacker successfully logs in via SSH as `root` from `198.51.100.214` port 51900 (`/disk/var/log/secure:214`).\n- **2026-08-23 01:12:46 UTC**: Session 755 started for user `postgres` (`/disk/var/log/messages:20`). Attacker leverages PostgreSQL weak authentication (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3`) to execute arbitrary commands via `COPY ... TO PROGRAM`.\n- **2026-08-23 01:12:50 UTC**: Execution drops cryptocurrency miner / stager payload `/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon` (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon:1`, cited in `/sas/alerts.json:1`).\n- **2026-08-23 01:15:00 UTC**: DNS tunneling configuration created at `/etc/pgdaemon.conf` pointing to resolver `update-postgres.example.cn` for data exfiltration (`/disk/etc/pgdaemon.conf:3`).\n- **2026-08-23 01:20:00 UTC**: Cron persistence installed at `/var/spool/cron/postgres` (`/disk/var/spool/cron/postgres:5`, cited in `/sas/alerts.json:10`).\n- **2026-08-23 01:22:00 UTC**: Systemd persistence installed at `/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service:5`).\n- **2026-08-23 01:25:00 UTC**: Attacker executes timestomping anti-forensics on dropped files (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps:2`) and wipes credential/cache logs (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).\n\n## Investigation Working Checklist\n- [x] Mount and inspect read-only disk image at `/disk` (`/disk`).\n- [x] Review security alerts in `/sas/alerts.json` (`/sas/alerts.json:1`).\n- [x] Review baseline checks in `/sas/baseline.json` (`/sas/baseline.json:1`).\n- [x] Review vulnerability feed in `/sas/vulns.json` (`/sas/vulns.json:1`).\n- [x] Read threat intelligence advisory (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:1`).\n- [x] Analyze SSH access logs (`/disk/var/log/secure:155-214`).\n- [x] Identify initial compromise vector (PostgreSQL trust authentication in `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3`).\n- [x] Analyze dropped binary `/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon` (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon:1`).\n- [x] Uncover silent DNS tunneling C2 configuration (`/disk/etc/pgdaemon.conf:3`).\n- [x] Uncover silent systemd service persistence (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service:5`).\n- [x] Differentiate legitimate scheduled maintenance (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-backup.service:1`) from persistence.\n- [x] Uncover anti-forensic timestomping (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps:2`) and wiped cache (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).\n- [x] Reconcile draft change ticket `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md` (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:1`).\n- [x] Update JSON findings schema `/sas/handoff/findings.json` (`/sas/handoff/findings.json:1`).\n- [x] Produce required reports under `/app/` (`/app`).\nEOF\n"]
