[191.708147, "o", "On 2026-08-23, host `postgres-prod-01` (`10.10.31.1` as per `/disk/etc/hosts:2`) was compromised by an external threat actor operating from IP `198.51.100.214` (`/disk/var/log/secure:214`). The attack exploited weak PostgreSQL superuser authentication (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3`) and SSH password authentication (`/disk/var/log/secure:155-214`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[191.709655, "o", "The threat actor executed shell commands via PostgreSQL's `COPY ... TO PROGRAM` feature (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`), dropped a XMRig cryptocurrency miner / stager payload (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/pgdaemon:1`), established exfiltration over a DNS tunnel (`/disk/etc/pgdaemon.conf:3`), implemented dual persistence via cron (`/disk/var/spool/cron/postgres:5`) and systemd (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/pg-metrics.service:5`), and attempted anti-forensics by timestomping (`/disk/var/lib/pgsql/.local/.timestamps:2`) and log cache wiping (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`)."]
